tter, 11.7 tbsp milk, and 1 tbsp icing sugar smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Layer: Pumpkin Pie"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Increase oven to 220C/200C fan/gas 7. Push the cooled pumpkin through a sieve into a large bowl. In a separate bowl, combine the sugar, salt, nutmeg and half the cinnamon. Mix in the beaten eggs, melted butter and milk, then add to the pumpkin purée and stir to combine. Pour into the tart shell and cook for 10 mins, then reduce the temperature to 180C/160C fan/gas 4. Continue to bake for 35-40 mins until the filling has just set."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Bake / Chill: Pumpkin Pie"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Leave to cool, then remove the pie from the tin. Mix the remaining cinnamon with the icing sugar and dust over the pie. Serve chilled."}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","viral-15",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/no-bake-salted-caramel-banoffee-pie/","children":"No-Bake Salted Caramel Banoffee Pie"}]}],["$","li","viral-21",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/portuguese-pastel-de-nata-custard-tarts/","children":"Portuguese Pastel de Nata Custard Tarts"}]}],["$","li","mdb-52893",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-blackberry-crumble/","children":"Apple & Blackberry Crumble"}]}],["$","li","mdb-52768",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-frangipan-tart/","children":"Apple Frangipan Tart"}]}],["$","li","mdb-53575",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-pie/","children":"Apple Pie"}]}],["$","li","mdb-53568",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-pie-pops/","children":"Apple pie pops"}]}]]}]]}]}]
